{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Hear</b> — At the beginning he mentioned, 'I removed the burden from Israel's shoulder'; therefore he is obligated to heed Me. It is written here: 'There shall not be in you a strange El' — a strange El is not to be found in you, that is, in the beliefs of the heart. And in the second utterance it is written: 'There shall not be to you [other] Elohim.' The interpretation is: from the mouth of the sage, 'in you' means not found in deed, and 'to you' means not in the belief of the heart."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:42.638223500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}